# This repo is the DEPLOYED SITE ONLY. Netlify publishes whatever is here, and
# the repo is public — so anything committed is public.
#
# The working project lives separately at ~/flash-cards-dinshi/ and holds the
# source material and build tooling. None of that belongs here: it is either
# large (the lesson recordings are 15MB, the course PDFs 11MB), not the site's
# to serve (the teacher's original course material), or simply noise.
#
# Only four things should ever be in this repo:
#   index.html       the built page
#   audio/           the word clips the cards play
#   netlify.toml     build config (secret-scanner settings — do not delete)
#   netlify/         the Speech proxy function

# ── the teacher's source material — large, and his, not the site's ──────
lesson-recordings/
lesson-pdfs/
*.pdf

# ── build tooling and working data (lives in ~/flash-cards-dinshi/app) ──
app/
build_flashcards.py
pronunciation/
*.py
*.csv
audio-manifest.json

# ── local preview scaffolding — must never reach production ────────────
preview.html
preview-data.csv

# ── project docs / backups that aren't part of the site ────────────────
claude-skill/
claude-memory/
pending-import/
archive/
firebase/
git/
to-deploy/
upload-batches/

# ── OS / editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── credentials: nothing of the sort should ever be committed ──────────
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
netlify/functions/.env
